import{_ as a,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 894 | Transcended Ones and Diplomacy | Law Basis of Cross-Plane Diplomacy","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 894 | Transcended Ones and Diplomacy | Law Basis of Cross-Plane Diplomacy","no":894,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Diplomacy","Cross-Plane","Law Basis","Law-First Axiom"],"related":["28-Cross-Plane Anchor Connection","13-Spatial-Law Dispatch System Details","812-Law-Anchor Authority at Hyper-Multiverse Scale","893-Transcended Ones and Diplomacy Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0894_模块4-超脱者与外交-跨位面外交的法则基础.md","filePath":"en/0894_模块4-超脱者与外交-跨位面外交的法则基础.md"}'),t={name:"en/0894_模块4-超脱者与外交-跨位面外交的法则基础.md"};function s(l,e,r,c,h,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-894-transcended-ones-and-diplomacy-law-basis-of-cross-plane-diplomacy" tabindex="-1">Entry 894 | Transcended Ones and Diplomacy | Law Basis of Cross-Plane Diplomacy <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-894-transcended-ones-and-diplomacy-law-basis-of-cross-plane-diplomacy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 894 | Transcended Ones and Diplomacy | Law Basis of Cross-Plane Diplomacy&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 28, 13, 812, 893</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-diplomacy-is-not-a-banquet-—-it-is-docking-at-the-law-level" tabindex="-1">Introduction: diplomacy is not a banquet — it is docking at the law level <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-diplomacy-is-not-a-banquet-—-it-is-docking-at-the-law-level" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: diplomacy is not a banquet — it is docking at the law level&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cross-plane diplomacy is not as simple as envoys from two states visiting each other; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning. Different planes&#39; law frameworks are completely different; two civilizations wanting to dialogue must first solve &quot;how to dock at the law level.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s cross-plane diplomacy is built on a rigorous law basis. This entry explains this basis.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the law-first axiom is this entry&#39;s core — diplomatic agreements must be self-consistent at the law level; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires law docking serve equal dialogue; the anti-predation axiom requires law docking not be manipulated by one side; the collective ascension axiom requires law docking promote common evolution; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the law-docking process be traceable.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-law-differences-between-different-planes" tabindex="-1">I. Law Differences Between Different Planes <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-law-differences-between-different-planes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Law Differences Between Different Planes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cross-plane diplomacy&#39;s first problem is: different planes&#39; laws are fundamentally different.</p><ul><li><strong>Different energy laws</strong>: Plane A&#39;s spiritual energy may not exist at all on Plane B;</li><li><strong>Different time laws</strong>: Plane A&#39;s one day may be one year on Plane B;</li><li><strong>Different consciousness laws</strong>: Plane A&#39;s individual consciousness may be collective consciousness on Plane B;</li><li><strong>Different causal laws</strong>: Plane A&#39;s causal lines may not hold on Plane B.</li></ul><p>These differences mean: <strong>beings from two planes cannot directly understand each other.</strong> Not language mismatch, but law-level mismatch.</p><h2 id="ii-the-three-layer-law-docking-protocol" tabindex="-1">II. The Three-Layer Law-Docking Protocol <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-three-layer-law-docking-protocol" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Three-Layer Law-Docking Protocol&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou solves the law-docking problem through a three-layer protocol:</p><h3 id="layer-1-law-translation-layer" tabindex="-1">Layer 1: Law translation layer <a class="header-anchor" href="#layer-1-law-translation-layer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Layer 1: Law translation layer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The transcended one is responsible for &quot;translating&quot; one plane&#39;s law framework into an expression another plane may understand:</p><ul><li>Energy-conversion protocol: how different planes&#39; energy forms are equivalently converted;</li><li>Time-synchronization protocol: how planes with different time flows coordinate schedules;</li><li>Consciousness-mapping protocol: how beings with different consciousness structures understand each other.</li></ul><h3 id="layer-2-law-compatibility-layer" tabindex="-1">Layer 2: Law compatibility layer <a class="header-anchor" href="#layer-2-law-compatibility-layer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Layer 2: Law compatibility layer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>On the basis of translation, design a law framework under which two planes may coexist:</p><ul><li>Cross-plane passage protocol: how laws adapt when one side enters the other&#39;s plane;</li><li>Cross-plane trade protocol: law rules for cross-plane energy and matter transmission;</li><li>Cross-plane legal protocol: which set of laws applies to disputes.</li></ul><h3 id="layer-3-law-anchoring-layer" tabindex="-1">Layer 3: Law anchoring layer <a class="header-anchor" href="#layer-3-law-anchoring-layer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Layer 3: Law anchoring layer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Ultimately, through the anchor network (Document 28), connect two planes&#39; law frameworks:</p><ul><li>Anchor connection point: a stable channel between two planes;</li><li>Law arbitration mechanism: when laws conflict, the Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision arbitrate;</li><li>Joint law revision: major law changes require mutual consultation.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-the-law-first-axiom-s-execution-in-diplomacy" tabindex="-1">III. The Law-First Axiom&#39;s Execution in Diplomacy <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-law-first-axiom-s-execution-in-diplomacy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Law-First Axiom&#39;s Execution in Diplomacy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom&#39;s expression in cross-plane diplomacy is:</p><ul><li><strong>Diplomatic agreements must be feasible at the law level</strong>: may not sign an agreement that is &quot;law-level impossible&quot;;</li><li><strong>Law self-consistency takes precedence over diplomatic convenience</strong>: may not neglect law conflicts for diplomatic results;</li><li><strong>Law revision must follow proper procedure</strong>: may not temporarily alter laws because of diplomatic needs;</li><li><strong>Alaya verifies diplomatic agreements</strong>: before signing, the agreement must pass causal-impact assessment.</li></ul><p>This means: diplomacy is not whatever the transcended one wants to sign — what he signs must stand at the law level.</p><h2 id="iv-the-diplomatic-agreement-s-life-cycle" tabindex="-1">IV. The Diplomatic Agreement&#39;s Life Cycle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-diplomatic-agreement-s-life-cycle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Diplomatic Agreement&#39;s Life Cycle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A cross-plane diplomatic agreement is not finished once signed; it has a complete life cycle:</p><ol><li><strong>Observation period</strong>: first observe the other plane&#39;s law characteristics through the Alaya Network;</li><li><strong>Design period</strong>: design the law-docking plan;</li><li><strong>Negotiation period</strong>: both sides negotiate agreement clauses;</li><li><strong>Signing period</strong>: formally sign, Alaya records;</li><li><strong>Execution period</strong>: execute per agreement, Alaya supervises;</li><li><strong>Revision period</strong>: revise the agreement based on execution;</li><li><strong>Exit period</strong>: agreement expires or both sides agree to terminate.</li></ol><p>Each stage has law-level checkpoints, ensuring the agreement does not collapse due to law conflicts.</p><p>The difficulty of law docking is often underestimated. Beings from two planes may not even share the concept of &quot;time&quot; — Plane A feels time is linear; Plane B feels time is cyclic. The transcended one must find a dialogue basis between such fundamental differences; this is harder than translating any language.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law docking greatly lowers cross-plane exchange costs</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: law agreements ensure cross-plane trade does not become predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo needs no law docking — he alone crushes all planes; Heng Yuan Zhou must design a law framework for every diplomatic partner</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: law-docking protocols are customized for five Myriad-Rank-lineage life forms</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: law-docking agreement full texts and technical documents open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cross-plane diplomacy&#39;s law basis is the three-layer protocol of law translation, law compatibility, law anchoring. It ensures civilizations from different planes may dialogue, cooperate, and coexist at the law level. Diplomacy is not a banquet; it is law engineering — every word signed must stand at the law level. The law-first axiom here means: diplomatic results may not come at the cost of law self-consistency. This is the orthodox definition of cross-plane diplomacy&#39;s law basis.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/13-空间法理调度体系详解.html">Entry 13 · Spatial-Law Dispatch System Details</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/812_模块4-超脱者与法则-法则锚定权限超多元尺度.html">Entry 812 · Law-Anchor Authority at Hyper-Multiverse Scale</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/893_模块4-超脱者与外交-总论.html">Entry 893 · Transcended Ones and Diplomacy Overview</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const u=a(t,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
